---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/help.css';

const city = 'https://westbrookmaine.gov';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Election Results | Westbrook Currents"
  description="Results are still being counted for the November 3, 2026 general election in Westbrook, Maine. Check back soon."
  currentPage="vote"
>
  <main class="help-wrap t-vote">
    <a class="help-back" href="/">&#8249; Home</a>
    <h1>Election Results</h1>
    <p class="help-sub">General Election &middot; Tuesday, November 3, 2026</p>

    <section class="vote-hero" aria-label="Results pending">
      <small>Counting in progress</small>
      <strong>We're still waiting on the final count.</strong>
      <p>Polls have closed, but official results aren't in yet. Check back here soon &mdash; we'll post results once they're final.</p>
      <p>Based on past elections, most local races are usually reported by the morning after Election Day (Wednesday, Nov. 4). Statewide races using ranked choice voting can take longer if no candidate wins a majority outright.</p>
      <a class="btn" href={`${city}/589/Election-Results`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City's live results page<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span> &#8599;</a>
    </section>

    <section class="help-box" aria-labelledby="why-title">
      <h2 id="why-title">Why the wait?</h2>
      <p>Election workers count ballots by hand, including absentee ballots that came in right up to the 8 p.m. deadline, and send unofficial totals to the Secretary of State as soon as they're done &mdash; usually the same night or the next morning.</p>
      <p>Official, certified results can take longer. The State has up to 20 days to certify a race, and any race decided by ranked choice voting, or close enough to call for a recount, can take noticeably longer than that.</p>
    </section>

    <aside class="disclaimer" aria-label="About this page">
      <strong>Thank you to everyone who voted, and to the election workers.</strong> Westbrook Currents is independent and is not run by the City of Westbrook. We'll share the final results here once they're certified.
    </aside>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
